IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`

-- g8-penalties: the penalties of the three offences of group G8 (Articles 26(7), 26(10), 29(1)) as data, and the one question the data cannot answer alone:
-- whether a term of imprisonment is within the maximum, which depends on the reading of the unit (F8.8, IP35).
-- An offence is a prohibition with its penalty as data (BRIEF ruling 6).  The Law states a maximum for no fine in money: 26(7) says "level 3 on the standard scale",
-- whose amount is not in the sources, and 26(10) and 29(1) say only "a fine".  So no amount of fine is computed, and the amount is a named refusal.

§ `Part 7 -- Penalties`

§§ `Article 26(7) -- the penalty`

-- src:632 | (7) A person who without reasonable excuse contravenes a requirement imposed on the person under paragraph (1) or (4), commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of 3 months and to a fine of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref Article 26(7) (src:632)
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 26(7) the penalty provided for the offence` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 3), (`a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3)

-- The maximum of a fine of level 3 is not in the sources.  A named refusal, returned (not stored) so that nothing downstream can default it.
@ref Article 26(7) (src:632)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 26(7) the amount of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale` MEANS
    REFUSE "the amount of level 3 on the standard scale is not in the sources"

§§ `Article 26(10) -- the penalty`

-- src:635 | (10) A person commits an offence, and is liable to imprisonment for a term of 2 years and to a fine, if the person provides information to the Commissioner, knowing that it is false in a material particular and intending it to be used by the Commissioner for the purpose of an application for registration or for the purpose of determining whether to serve a required steps notice.
@ref Article 26(10) (src:635)
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 26(10) the penalty provided for the offence` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

@ref Article 26(10) (src:635)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 26(10) the maximum fine` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 26(10) states no maximum for the fine"

§§ `Article 29(1) -- the penalty`

-- src:667 | commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine if he or she discloses the information without the consent of the person to whom it relates and (where sub-paragraph (b) applies) the person from whom it was received.
@ref Article 29(1) (src:667)
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`Art 29(1) the penalty provided for the offence` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

@ref Article 29(1) (src:667)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 29(1) the maximum fine` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 29(1) states no maximum for the fine"

§§ `Articles 26 and 29 -- is a term of imprisonment within the maximum (F8.8)`

-- The Law writes "3 months" (26(7)) and "2 years" (26(10), 29(1)).  The calendar reading takes the Law's unit as a calendar period from the start of the term;
-- the days reading takes 3 months as 90 days and 2 years as 730 days.  The days figures belong to that reading alone: the Law does not say a month is 30 days or a year 365.
-- They are written here as the two readings' own constants, so that a sentence can be tested against either.

@ref Articles 26(7), 26(10) and 29(1) (src:632) (src:635) (src:667)
GIVEN offence IS AN `Offence under Article 26 or 29`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in calendar months` offence MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `the offence of contravening a requirement under Article 26(1) or (4)` THEN 3
    WHEN `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` THEN 24
    WHEN `the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1)` THEN 24

@ref Articles 26(7), 26(10) and 29(1) (src:632) (src:635) (src:667)
GIVEN offence IS AN `Offence under Article 26 or 29`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in days on the days reading` offence MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `the offence of contravening a requirement under Article 26(1) or (4)` THEN 90
    WHEN `the offence of providing false information under Article 26(10)` THEN 730
    WHEN `the offence of disclosing restricted information under Article 29(1)` THEN 730

-- Reading A (taken): the term, counted from the day it starts, must end no later than the same day the stated number of calendar months on (clamped at a month end by `add months`).
@ref Articles 26(7), 26(10) and 29(1) (src:632) (src:635) (src:667)
GIVEN offence IS AN `Offence under Article 26 or 29`
      start IS A DATE
      length IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 26 and 29 reading A: a term within the calendar months` offence start length MEANS
    (start PLUS length) AT MOST `add months` start (`Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in calendar months` offence)

-- Reading B: the term must not be longer than the number of days.
@ref Articles 26(7), 26(10) and 29(1) (src:632) (src:635) (src:667)
GIVEN offence IS AN `Offence under Article 26 or 29`
      length IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 26 and 29 reading B: a term within the days` offence length MEANS
    length AT MOST `Art 26 and 29 the maximum term in days on the days reading` offence

@ref Articles 26(7), 26(10) and 29(1) (src:632) (src:635) (src:667)
@export Whether a term of imprisonment that starts on a given day and lasts a given number of days is within the maximum the Law provides for the offence, on the reading of the unit given (default - calendar months)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` @desc The readings of the forks of Articles 26 to 36; the unit of a term of imprisonment is the field F8.8
      offence IS AN `Offence under Article 26 or 29` @desc Which offence: contravening an Article 26 requirement (3 months), false information under Article 26(10) (2 years) or disclosure under Article 29(1) (2 years)
      start IS A DATE @desc The day the term of imprisonment starts
      length IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the term lasts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` interp offence start length MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `unit of the terms of imprisonment in Articles 26 and 29`
    WHEN `calendar months` THEN `Art 26 and 29 reading A: a term within the calendar months` offence start length
    WHEN `days` THEN `Art 26 and 29 reading B: a term within the days` offence length
